  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "If \\(x\\ne y\\) and the sequences \\(x,\\) \\(a_1,\\) \\(a_2,\\) \\(y\\) and \\(x,\\) \\(b_1,\\) \\(b_2,\\) \\(b_3,\\) \\(y\\) each are in arithmetic progression, then \\(\\frac{a_2-a_1}{b_2-b_1}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac23\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac34\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac43\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac32\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "An arithmetic progression has equal differences between consecutive terms. The first progression goes from \\(x\\) to \\(y\\) in three equal gaps, whereas the second does so in four. Therefore\n\\[\na_2-a_1=\\frac{y-x}{3},\\qquad\nb_2-b_1=\\frac{y-x}{4}.\n\\]\nSince \\(x\\ne y\\), the second difference is nonzero, and we may cancel the common factor \\(y-x\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{a_2-a_1}{b_2-b_1}\n=\\frac{(y-x)/3}{(y-x)/4}\n=\\frac43.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac43\\), choice D.",
